{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>As this day.</b> Close to this day. The truth is that it hints at what they inherited, the land of the two kings of the Amorites, for Reuben, Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh are called Israel, and so it is written: \"as Israel did to the land of his inheritance.\" It is not a future matter as many interpreted it. The witness: He struck great kings — in the psalm \"Give thanks to YHWH for He is good\" he mentioned only Sihon and Og, and said: \"a heritage to Israel His servant.\" And after he said: \"for YHWH, He is the Elohim, there is none else besides Him,\" he said a weighty reason: for the first proof is from the sight of the eyes, and by weighing the understanding and by the wisdom of the heart you shall know that HaShem alone is Elohim in the heavens above — they are above the son of man — and upon the earth that is beneath it. The witness, that so he interpreted: \"and your heavens that are over your head [shall be] bronze.\" And after you saw the awesome deeds and you return to your heart, you are obligated to keep His commandments; also it is good for you and for your children after you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase במזמור הודו לה' כי טוב introduces a citation from Psalm 136; the specific verse references within it and to Deuteronomy are left implicit by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:24.059664075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}